    "result_text": "Done. Tests remain green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I addressed\n\n**Primary finding \u2014 stale `OwnerNames` javadoc (agreed, fixed).** The review is correct: `FlagPossibleDuplicate` no longer calls `OwnerNames.normalize` (it now matches on `Owner.soundex`), so the class doc claiming it as a consumer was misleading. I rewrote the doc to state `CountNamesakes` is its only consumer and added a cross-reference pointing phonetic last-name matching to `Owner.soundex`.\n\n**Secondary \u2014 soundex placement (agreed with the review's own conclusion; added the suggested comment).** The reviewer concluded keeping `soundex` on `Owner` is the right call given `getIdentityKey()` can't reach into the package-private `rest.function.owner` layer without inverting the dependency. I left the placement as-is and expanded the `Owner.soundex` javadoc to explicitly acknowledge *why* it lives on the entity and that it's a distinct concern (phonetic keying) from `OwnerNames` (exact comparison), so the two name utilities don't silently drift.\n\n**Secondary \u2014 scan-loop boilerplate.** The review itself marked this \"no change required\" under the one-function-per-step idiom, and I agree \u2014 extracting a shared scan helper would couple two steps that legitimately do different things (throw vs. flag), so I left it.\n\nAll changes this round were documentation-only; no behaviour changed.",
