    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new endpoint, exception, handler, and YAML all follow the OfficeFloor conventions cleanly, and reusing the existing `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper in the handler is the right call. The structure is almost there, but the change leaves one coherence defect:\n\n**`OwnerNames` javadoc is now stale (`OwnerNames.java:8-10`).** That class documents itself as the \"Single source of truth for what a 'normalized' owner name ... is for comparison ... Shared by the steps that compare names across owners (`CountNamesakes` counts namesakes, **`FlagPossibleDuplicate` matches last name**).\" This diff rewires `FlagPossibleDuplicate` to match on `Owner.soundex(...)` and drops its `OwnerNames.normalize` usage entirely \u2014 `FlagPossibleDuplicate` is no longer a consumer of `OwnerNames` at all (only `CountNamesakes` is now). A maintainer reading `OwnerNames` will be actively misled about where last-name phonetic matching lives. Update the javadoc to drop the `FlagPossibleDuplicate` reference, and consider noting that phonetic last-name matching now lives in `Owner.soundex`.\n\nSecondary (not blocking):\n\n- **Soundex placement.** Name-comparison logic is now split: `normalize` in `OwnerNames`, `soundex` on the `Owner` entity. Ideally last-name phonetic keying would sit beside `normalize` in `OwnerNames`, but that class is package-private in `rest.function.owner` and `getIdentityKey()` legitimately lives on the entity (consistent with the other `@Transient` derived getters), so the model can't reach it without an inverted layer dependency. Given that constraint, keeping `soundex` on `Owner` is defensible \u2014 just worth a comment acknowledging it's the shared phonetic key so the two name utilities don't silently drift.\n\n- **Scan-loop boilerplate** (`DetectDuplicateIdentity` / `FlagPossibleDuplicate`): both repeat the `findAll()` \u2192 skip-null-id \u2192 skip-deleted iteration. This is acceptable under the one-function-per-step idiom since the steps do genuinely different things; no change required.",
